 "notes": "Curve traced from the vector inset of Fig. 4 (plots/dp_limplot_V6.pdf in the e-print): lower envelope of the 90%-CL excluded region (bottoms of the 28 exclusion bands spanning 6.000-6.022 GHz, i.e. 24.81-24.91 ueV, with the on-resonance band at 6.011 GHz resolved into its V-profile). Whole curve anchored (0.04-decade shift) so the on-resonance minimum equals the quoted headline epsilon = 1.68e-15 at m = 24.86 ueV. The excluded region is actually a set of narrow disjoint bands (sensitivity at odd multiples of 2*chi qubit shift); the reported curve is the envelope through the band minima (the paper's dashed guide line). Exclusion also extends only up to epsilon ~ 3e-8 (large-amplitude cutoff), not reported here. rho_DM = 0.4 GeV/cm^3 assumed by the paper; mass = h*frequency with h = 4.13567e-15 eV/Hz.",
